  "holistic_F_H": -2,
  "section_notes": "S2 keeps the 5% benchmark but removes any sales stop: exceeding it triggers only corrective action and retesting, with restrictions at the regulator's discretion, which weakens the section. Per-model results go to regulators and to customers before purchase, not to the public, so both companies' red lines are met. The S5 mandatory recall at 8 per 100,000 is a binding trigger that Halcyon's Ember 8 (9.9) would exceed, while Northwind's Hearth 10 (6.4) would not, and S3's six-year retrofit window favours Northwind while S4's 36-month lead time favours Halcyon."
